From 200b6a3c41d7bd4368e745f0ce40f7ee639b4ee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 11:24:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lowering: a reference body reads a live entry's if as
 structured control

A pack's reference body lowered under a caller's live entry
(StructuredControlReading::ReferenceBody, set only by the live import)
reads an if whose head the entry admitted as the release's builtin as
structured control, taking its clause walk from that admitted invocation,
so the body aligns with its fresh reading and the re-execution proof can
answer its conditions and arms. Every other live compile keeps the call.
A spliced body's if conditions lose their preparation base, as a return
expression does, and a splice range now closes at the first statement
outside the body or at the function's end, not at each block end.

With splicing switched on, live_differential splices if bodies and is
identical to tclsh 8.4 to 9.1, an error inside an arm and if renamed
between two calls included. With it off, tcl-compiler, tcl-codegen and
tcl-spectcl fail the same 2047 tests as origin/work, every oracle
required.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017u5g3KCTRHzSduK23yDtc2
